WEBVTT

NOTE Avatar captions follow the real captured app answer. Narrator captions identify separate editorial speech.

1
00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:03.773
[Avatar] Looking at the worksheet, it looks like
you have four main colors to work with.

2
00:00:04.113 --> 00:00:06.153
[Avatar] Green, yellow, blue, and white.

3
00:00:06.493 --> 00:00:10.553
[Avatar] To start, you could try counting how
many shapes fall into each color group.

4
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:15.096
[Narrator] Ask your question out loud. Speak
transcribes it and sends it for you.

5
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:24.055
[Narrator] Homework in another tab? Capture a
screenshot, then ask about what you see.

6
00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:36.547
[Avatar] That is a great idea. Sorting by the
number of squares is a perfect way to practice
looking at the properties of the shapes.

7
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:40.219
[Narrator] Zoom in on the diagram to see every
detail.

8
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:46.312
[Narrator] Your conversation stays together,
ready for the next question.

9
00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:55.107
[Avatar] The shape might look different to your
eyes, but the actual amount of space it covers
doesn't change.

